                    {
                        "sense_id": "d6c07482-afca-3615-acc3-b42af3fea7d0",
                        "entry_id": "23c53632-7a17-3369-8e16-66b2cb98204d",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Having some specific type of cheek."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "in-compounds",
                            "not-comparable",
                            "usually"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "72388520-197c-4ed3-97dc-a93552163e20",
                                "sense_id": "d6c07482-afca-3615-acc3-b42af3fea7d0",
                                "text": "Oh here be rare apples, red-cheeked apples that cry come kiss me: apples, hold your peace, I'll teach you to cry. [Eats one."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "f2e8deec-7633-406b-b92c-17b01282bf63",
                                "sense_id": "d6c07482-afca-3615-acc3-b42af3fea7d0",
                                "text": "1771, Miguel de Cervantes, The History of the Renowned Don Quixote de la Mancha, translators not credited, London: W. Cowper, Vol. III, p. 87, https://books.google.ca/books?id=v80ZAAAAYAAJ&printsec=frontcover#v=onepage&q&f=false\n[…] and perceiving her to be no more than a plain country-wench, so far from being well-favoured, that she was blubber-cheeked, and flat-nosed, he was lost in astonishment, and could not utter a word."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "feb36334-748a-4a39-a079-a39eb3f35b3f",
                                "sense_id": "d6c07482-afca-3615-acc3-b42af3fea7d0",
                                "text": "I pictured to myself some grizzled, apple-cheeked, country schoolmaster fluting in his bit of garden in the clear autumn sunshine."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "8df9c9c5-0a6e-4dc2-a318-02f7d54d68db",
                                "sense_id": "d6c07482-afca-3615-acc3-b42af3fea7d0",
                                "text": "Time is jealous of you, and wars against your lilies and your roses. You will become sallow, and hollow-cheeked, and dull-eyed. You will suffer horribly...."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "540bd745-d3e2-4172-bbe7-f2d32e9eba6b",
                                "sense_id": "d6c07482-afca-3615-acc3-b42af3fea7d0",
                                "text": "Past rivers and hills she went, and met a bushy-cheeked tiger on the path […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "bcd3471e-2983-4373-873c-6f99e39afcc2",
                                "sense_id": "d6c07482-afca-3615-acc3-b42af3fea7d0",
                                "text": "The earliest painting that can be attributed to his reign is of a plump, rosy-cheeked adolescent wearing a splendid conical turban and a huge emerald necklace."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
